course: dictionary
lesson: 1835
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. «Cobalt» can name a metal, or it can be part of a colour, as in «cobalt blue». Look at the clues: you can hold a metal in your hand, but a colour is something you see on a bowl or a wall.
explain: Cobalt is a hard, silvery-grey metal, and it is a chemical element, which means one of the basic substances that other things are made from. Read «The bowl was cobalt blue.» Blue is a clue that cobalt is a colour here, not a metal.
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. «The bowl was silvery-grey metal» does not make sense, so the colour meaning is right. Always test your meaning before you decide.
fact: Cobalt is a hard, silvery-grey metal and a chemical element.
fact: Cobalt blue is a deep, bright blue colour, made from cobalt and used in paints and glass.
fact: «Only iron, steel, nickel and cobalt are pulled strongly» by a magnet, so cobalt is magnetic.
fact: Cobalt is used in strong magnets, batteries and tough tools.
fact: Some words, like «cobalt», are a noun for a thing and also part of a describing phrase, so the clues around them matter.
exercise: «Your phone holds metals dug from mines, such as lithium, cobalt, copper and gold.» What is cobalt in this sentence? | A kind of fruit | *A metal, dug from a mine | A bird that cannot fly | A type of cloth
exercise: «The little vase was painted cobalt blue.» What does cobalt blue mean here? | A pale pink | A hard, silvery-grey metal | *A deep, bright blue colour
exercise: «Only iron, steel, nickel and cobalt are pulled strongly by a magnet.» What does this tell you about cobalt? | *It is magnetic | It is a kind of bread | It can be eaten with a spoon
test: Which of these is a use of cobalt? | Cooking eggs | *Strong magnets | Making bread | Growing trees
test: Ella reads «The bowl was cobalt blue.» Does cobalt mean a metal here? | Yes, it means a soft wool | *No, it is a colour: cobalt blue | No, it means a small bird | Yes, a bowl is made of metal
exam: Which sentence uses cobalt to mean the metal? | *«A magnet pulls iron, steel, nickel and cobalt.» | «Her scarf was a deep cobalt.» | «The wall was painted cobalt blue.»
